+"""Orbit measurements for a test particle in a central force field.
+
+The radial period of a bound orbit is the time between two successive closest
+approaches to the origin (periapsis passages).  Because the force law is only
+known through the callable ``accel``, the equations of motion are integrated
+numerically and the passages are located as the zeros of ``d(r**2)/dt``.
+
+The integration uses a Dormand-Prince 5(4) adaptive Runge-Kutta scheme, which
+needs no third-party dependencies.  Closest approaches are detected as places
+where ``x*vx + y*vy`` crosses zero from below (a minimum of ``r``) and their
+times are refined by bisection on a freshly integrated arc.
+"""
+
+import math
 
 
